==Strategy==
This is a relatively straightforward stage. Bring meatshields ([[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] for 1-3 Crowns), something to stall Oldhorn (e.g. [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]], [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]], etc.), then some damage dealers, at least one with Area Attack (e.g. [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], Talented [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]).

As long as you manage your money well, you should be able to pin the Oldhorns in place for long enough to not allow them to stack, by killing each in time for the arrival of the next. Just remember to save up money and stall with cheap units when waiting for the next Oldhorn, as Nyandam will kill everything regardless. Once there are no more Oldhorns, chip away at Nyandam until he dies and you can win.

It is possible to kill Nyandam with [[Wave Attack|Waves]], [[Surge Attack|Surges]] or Long Distance attacks while there are Oldhorns alive. For this, it is recommended to bring along a Talented [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] or certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] you may have with the necessary requirements, in addition to [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]].

